[2.290364, "o", "\r\n"]
[2.428469, "o", "1. Stack up: the API, one worker, Postgres and a demo consumer.\r\n\r\n2. Sending 1,000 webhooks. Each gets a 202 once it's saved.\r\n"]
[4.822111, "o", "\r\n3. Worker killed with SIGKILL mid-delivery. No chance to clean up.\r\n   By then: 662 acknowledged, 143 delivered.\r\n"]
[8.862181, "o", "\r\n4. The API kept accepting: 338 more acknowledged after the kill.\r\n   Delivered stays at 143. The other 857 wait in Postgres.\r\n"]
[9.794134, "o", "\r\n5. New worker started. Anything the dead worker held comes back\r\n   when its 30-second lease runs out.\r\n"]
[9.808811, "o", "\r   Delivered: 143 of 1,000"]
[11.329413, "o", "\r   Delivered: 473 of 1,000"]
[11.839582, "o", "\r   Delivered: 923 of 1,000"]
[12.346174, "o", "\r   Delivered: 993 of 1,000"]
[36.240068, "o", "\r   Delivered: 1,000 of 1,000\r\n   The last 7 were held by the dead worker; they waited for its lease.\r\n"]
[36.240355, "o", "\r\n6. 1,000 acknowledged, 1,000 delivered, 0 lost.\r\n   1 delivered twice, same Webhook-Id, so the consumer drops them.\r\n"]
